@ahg-g This was brought up (#80921) to the table when PodTopologySpread was initially implemented. Back then, there were not enough data points showing which direction we wanted to head to. Another reason is TaintNodesByCondition and TaintBasedEvictions were not GA and thus extra logic was needed - both taints and conditions.

Node affinity is a hard requirement and explicitly related to topology domains, so it's intrusive to take it into consideration in the very beginning.

Overall I think it's a valid requirement, and I'm fine with excluding unscheduled taints (generated by k/k) in the PodTopologySpread feature.

```
type topologySpreadConstraint struct {
	MaxSkew        int32
	TopologyKey    string
	Selector       labels.Selector
	NodeExclustion nodeExclusion
}

type nodeExclusion struct {
	// default to true, same behavior as now
	respectNodeAffinity bool
	// default to true, same behavior as now
	respectNodeSelector bool
	taintStrategy       taintStrategy
}

type taintStrategyName string

const (
	// Default value, will ignore taints and taints of taintStrategy is nil. Same behavior as now for backward API compatibility.
	ignoreTaints taintStrategyName = "ignoreTaints"
	// Verify all taints in node and taints of taintStrategy is nil.
	respectAllTaints taintStrategyName = "respectAllTaints"
	// Only verify the taints included in the taints of taintStrategy, mull not be empty.
	respectExplicitTaints taintStrategyName = "respectExplicitTaints"
)

type taintStrategy struct {
	name   taintStrategyName
	taints []v1.Taint
}
```
what about this?

> do we really need to add the taints array today?

This is based on the support of system-level Unschedulable taints, while also keeping semantics explicit. If supporting Unschedulable taints is optional, or even unnecessary, we can simply the design with enums (respect/ignore), and evaluate the "custom" option (accompanied with a taints slice) in the future.

@nyarly, based on your usecase, it seems the option of system-level Unschedulable taints is not mandatory, can you confirm?
